# Recordings are build output, not source.
#
# They are reproducible from the code in this folder plus `npm run record`, and
# versioning them is expensive: 16-17 clips x ~5MB, rewritten on every re-record.
# In this repo that took .git to 140MB (138MB of it loose .webm objects) before
# the history was rewritten on 2026-08-19 with `git filter-repo --invert-paths
# --path-glob '*.webm'`, which brought it back to 672KB.
#
# Publish them as release assets or to a bucket instead of committing them.
#
# What IS tracked here is the manifest: `npm run manifest` writes manifest.json
# and MANIFEST.md recording each clip's date, hash, and whether the code it shows
# has changed since. That is how you tell a fresh recording from a stale one.
*.webm
!.gitignore

# Per-run outputs, written by the recorder and the pipeline. Like the clips they
# describe exactly one run, and the committed record is manifest.json /
# MANIFEST.md, not these.
RECORD_RESULTS*.json
RUN_REPORT.*
logs/
.temp_chunks/
